  "disclosures": [
    "Method choice: projections combine each county's own recent level with one national trend. In a strict out-of-time test (2021-2024 targets, no future data) this family had a mean absolute error of 15.7-16.8 CRI points, versus 17.9 for per-county linear trends, 18.1 for per-county Sen's slope and 20.3 for the last observed value.",
    "Window sensitivity: the level window (3, 5, 7 years, all years, or weighted) changes the test error by at most 1.1 points; the 5-year window is used.",
    "Over-projection: in the 2021-2024 test, projections were on average +2.3 CRI points above observed values, because the national trend slowed (from 1.56 points/yr at the 2020 origin to 0.94 at the 2023 origin).",
    "Regional accuracy: the West is least predictable (test error 19.1 points vs 13.8-15.7 elsewhere; 3-year 68% band covered 55% of Western outcomes vs 72-73% elsewhere). Region-specific trends were tested and did not improve accuracy.",
    "Band: the 68% band covered 70-74% of outcomes in the strict test (slightly conservative).",
    "Scope: the projection is a statistical reliability-risk index (relative to 2013-2024 county-years), not a prediction of actual outages, available capacity, or outage probability at a specific site. It cannot anticipate individual storms, utility investments or other events that change a county's trajectory."
  ],
